    "question": {
      "id": "f14ec8e3-78ca-490c-afcd-fb53de9e3d0a",
      "order": 3,
      "question": "Why did the gross margin decreased from 2018 to 2019?"
    },
    "selection": "First qualifying coarse-transfer event in version/source/step/question order, regardless of effect size. Offline labels shown for analysis only.",
    "source": {
      "id": "806ac467-ab50-428b-8584-baef6d6c4cee",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "order": 1,
          "text": "Year Ended December 31, 2019 Compared to Year Ended December 31, 2018"
        },
        {
          "order": 2,
          "text": "Operating revenues. Operating revenues decreased by 2.0% from NT$151,253 million in 2018 to NT$148,202 million (US$4,955 million) in\n2019, primarily due to decreased other operating revenues, decreased foundry wafer sale, and 2.5% depreciation of the NTD in 2019 from 2018. The decreased foundry wafer sale came from a decline of 2.9% in average selling price from 2018 to 2019, partially offset by a 1.1% increase in foundry wafer shipment from 7,108 thousand 8-inch equivalent wafers in 2018 to 7,189 thousand 8-inch equivalent wafers in 2019."
        },
        {
          "order": 3,
          "text": "Operating costs. Operating costs decreased by 1.2% from NT$128,413 million in 2018 to NT$126,887 million (US$4,242 million) in 2019, primarily due to the decreased depreciation expense and other operating costs, which was partially offset by the increased direct material costs."
        },
        {
          "order": 4,
          "text": "Gross profit and gross margin. Gross profit decreased from NT$22,840 million in 2018 to NT$21,315 million (US$713 million) in 2019. Our gross margin decreased from 15.1% in 2018 to 14.4% in 2019, primarily due to an annual decline of 2.9% in average selling price."
        }
      ],
